.TH AMERIKA-APPLY-DEFAULTS 1 "2026-10-21" "Amerika OS" "Amerika OS Manual"
.SH NAME
amerika\-apply\-defaults \- copy the Amerika application defaults into your dconf database
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B amerika\-apply\-defaults
.RB [ \-\-dry\-run | \-\-reset ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
The package
.B amerika\-defaults
ships GTK and GNOME\-stack defaults (dark colour scheme, icon theme, fonts, cursor, window button layout, wallpaper)
as the dconf database
.IR amerika .
The Amerika session selects it with
.BR DCONF_PROFILE=amerika .
If your session does not, this command writes the same keys into your own user database, so other sessions of your account
see them as well. It changes only the keys listed in
.IR /etc/dconf/db/amerika.d/00\-amerika .
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-dry\-run
Print the
.B dconf write
commands without running them.
.TP
.B \-\-reset
Reset exactly those keys to the system defaults.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR dconf (1),
.BR amerika\-flavour (7)
